1. Patient Registration
   - Patient creates an account with basic details.

2. Doctor Registration & Verification
   - Doctor registers and gets verified for secure access.

3. Login Process
   - Both patient and doctor log in using secure authentication.

4. Patient Record Creation
   - A unique digital record is created for each patient.

5. Data Entry (Patient Side)
   - Patient enters mood logs, daily activities, symptoms, and notes.

6. Record Update
   - New entries are added to the patient’s record regularly.

7. Data Encryption
   - All records and entries are encrypted before storage.

8. Secure Database Storage
   - Encrypted data is stored using a zero-knowledge system.

9. Enquiry Request (Doctor Side)
   - Doctor sends a request to access a patient’s record.

10. Permission Control (Patient Side)
    - Patient approves or denies doctor’s access request.

11. Record Access
    - Upon approval, doctor can view patient history and entries.

12. Risk Analysis Engine
    - System analyzes records to detect stress or abnormal patterns.

13. Alert Generation
    - Alerts are triggered for high-risk or unusual conditions.

14. Monitoring & Evaluation (Doctor)
    - Doctor reviews patient data and system-generated insights.

15. Feedback & Recommendation
    - Doctor provides suggestions, guidance, or treatment advice.

16. Audit Logging
    - All actions (entry, access, enquiry) are logged securely.

17. Data Modification Control
    - Only authorized updates are allowed; all changes are tracked.

18. Continuous Monitoring
    - System continuously updates analysis with new entries.

19. Patient Control Panel
    - Patient can view records, manage permissions, and track activity.

20. Secure Logout
    - Session ends safely, ensuring data protection.
